 {"q": "What does God say to Cain before the murder, and why does it matter?", "options": ["Nothing; Cain acts without warning", "That sin is crouching at the door but Cain can rule over it, so Cain was free and responsible", "That Cain is cursed already", "That Abel deserves to die"], "answer": 1, "why": "Genesis insists that wrongdoing is a choice, not a fate."},
 {"q": "Why is it significant that Cain builds the first city and names it after his son?", "options": ["It shows that cities are evil", "Far from God's presence, he makes a centre of his own with his family's name on it, a pattern Babel will repeat", "It proves that Cain repented", "It shows Cain was a skilled architect"], "answer": 1, "why": "A substitute centre; the Bible itself ends with a city, so the city is not bad in itself."},
